From: Joel Gerber <Jitsusama@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Find a Map's or a Set's string and number keys by hash

Qt 6.12.0's ESTable, behind Map, Set, WeakMap and WeakSet, finds a key
by comparing it with every key held, so has, get and set are linear and
filling one is quadratic: 1914 string keys took 11 to 22 ms to put in a
Set. String and number keys are now indexed by their hash as well as
held in insertion order; other keys, whose equality may be their own,
are compared in turn as before, and only while any are held.

---
--- a/src/qml/jsruntime/qv4estable.cpp
+++ b/src/qml/jsruntime/qv4estable.cpp
@@ -4,6 +4,9 @@
 
